Z||000002||Raydar||03-29-2001||01:55 PM||||I heard another discussion about AOL's proxy. No matter how many times you hit refresh, you're still only hitting the proxy. Not the actual server. <BR>Another AOHELL feature.<P><BR>Saw this post appear right away. <BR>You might check your cache settings, in AOL.<BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 03-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jaygee79||03-29-2001||02:29 PM||||If just refreshing doesn't work, then try holding down the CTRL key while clicking on refresh.  Works for me.||||reg||1
Z||000004||LZeitgeist||03-29-2001||02:45 PM||||Thanks guys - I had changed my settings to refresh automatically, and it evidently wasn't doing what it was supposed to be doing. Stupid computer. I changed it back to refreshing with every visit to the page and it's evidently working again. (BTW - the CTRL+Refresh worked great - I'll have to remember that one. Cool.)<P>Thanks again.||||reg||1
